  "prompt": "Compute\n$$\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\int_1^n\\frac{\\ln(x)}{n\\ln(n)}\\,dx.$$",
  "image": null,
  "choices": null,
  "answer": "1",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "L'Hopital",
    "body": "The limit is $\\lim\\frac{\\int_1^n\\ln x\\,dx}{n\\ln n}$, of type $\\infty/\\infty$. Differentiating numerator and denominator in $n$ gives $\\frac{\\ln n}{\\ln n+1}\\to1$.\n\n**Answer: 1**"
   },
   {
    "title": "Evaluate the integral",
    "body": "$\\int_1^n\\ln x\\,dx=n\\ln n-n+1$, so the ratio is $1-\\frac{n-1}{n\\ln n}\\to1$.\n\n**Answer: 1**"
   }
  ],
