  "type": "numeric",
  "prompt": "Let $f(x)=e^x\\sin(x)$. Compute $f^{(2022)}(0)$. Here, $f^{(2022)}(x)$ is the $2022$nd derivative of $f(x)$.",
  "image": null,
  "choices": null,
  "answer": "-2^1011",
  "acceptedAnswers": [
   "-2^{1011}",
   "-(2^1011)"
  ],
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Use complex exponentials",
    "body": "$f(x)=\\frac{e^{(1+i)x}-e^{(1-i)x}}{2i}$, so $f^{(2022)}(0)=\\frac{(1+i)^{2022}-(1-i)^{2022}}{2i}=\\operatorname{Im}\\left((1+i)^{2022}\\right)$.\n\n$(1+i)^{2022}=\\left(\\sqrt2\\right)^{2022}e^{i\\cdot2022\\pi/4}=2^{1011}e^{i\\cdot 3\\pi/2}$ (since $\\frac{2022\\pi}4=505\\pi+\\frac\\pi2\\equiv\\frac{3\\pi}2\\pmod{2\\pi}$), whose imaginary part is $-2^{1011}$.\n\n**Answer: $-2^{1011}$**"
   },
   {
    "title": "Repeated squaring",
    "body": "$(1+i)^2=2i$, so $(1+i)^{2022}=(2i)^{1011}=2^{1011}i^{1011}=2^{1011}\\cdot i^3=-2^{1011}i$. Imaginary part: $-2^{1011}$.\n\n**Answer: $-2^{1011}$**"
   }
  ],
