  "prompt": "Compute\n$$\\int_{1/e}^{e}\\frac{\\arctan(x)}x\\,dx.$$",
  "image": null,
  "choices": null,
  "answer": "pi/2",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "answerDisplay": "$\\frac\\pi2$",
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Symmetry",
    "body": "Let $x=e^u$: $I=\\int_{-1}^1\\arctan(e^u)\\,du$. Substituting $u\\to-u$ gives also $I=\\int_{-1}^1\\arctan(e^{-u})\\,du$. Adding and using $\\arctan y+\\arctan\\frac1y=\\frac\\pi2$ for $y>0$: $2I=\\int_{-1}^1\\frac\\pi2\\,du=\\pi$, so $I=\\frac\\pi2$.\n\n**Answer: $\\frac\\pi2$**"
   }
